Error vs Exception in Java
| Feature            | **Error**                                                 | **Exception**                                                  |
| ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Type**           | Serious issue in the **JVM or system**                    | Problem in **program logic** or **code**                       |
| **Can be Caught?** | ❌ Usually **cannot** be caught or handled                 | ✅ Can (and should) be **caught and handled** using `try-catch` |
| **Examples**       | `OutOfMemoryError`, `StackOverflowError`, `InternalError` | `NullPointerException`, `IOException`, `ArithmeticException`   |
| **When to Use**    | You typically **don’t handle errors** in your code        | You **handle exceptions** to recover from failure              |
| **Hierarchy**      | `java.lang.Error`                                         | `java.lang.Exception`                                          |
| **Subtypes**       | LinkageError, VirtualMachineError                         | RuntimeException, Checked Exceptions                           |


