    └── RuntimeException (e.g., NullPointerException)


🧪 Example of an Error
java
Copy
Edit
public class ErrorDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        causeError();
    }

    public static void causeError() {
        causeError(); // Causes StackOverflowError
    }
}
🔥 This causes a StackOverflowError — and you should NOT catch it.



✅ Example of an Exception
java
Copy
Edit
public class ExceptionDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            int result = 10 / 0; // ArithmeticException
        } catch (ArithmeticException e) {
            System.out.println("Cannot divide by zero.");
        }
    }
}
🧯 This causes an exception and you can handle it gracefully.

✅ Summary
| Criteria                     | Error              | Exception                     |
| ---------------------------- | ------------------ | ----------------------------- |
| Recoverable?                 | ❌ No               | ✅ Yes                         |
| Catchable?                   | ❌ Not usually      | ✅ Yes                         |
| Programmer's responsibility? | ❌ No               | ✅ Yes                         |
| Example                      | `OutOfMemoryError` | `IOException`                 |
| Best Practice                | Let JVM handle     | Catch and recover if possible |


